  "required_reader_corrections": [
    "Explain source E[X] exists as ordinary finite Lebesgue coordinate expectations, equivalent in finite-dimensional Euclidean space to genuine Bochner Integrable X via integrable_pi_iff/integrable_piLp_iff; exclude principal-value means and the total nonintegrable-zero fallback.",
    "State actual finite-dimensional real normed MeasurableSpace/BorelSpace scope, with no supplied CompleteSpace/inner-product parameter and no infinite-dimensional claim. Keep probability mass1 and separate Measurable f/Measurable X/Integrable X/AE domain assumptions visible.",
    "Distinguish one printed source theorem from its necessary negative-part producer. Producer measurability premises remain in the frozen type even if unused by its body. Historical compilation is not this migration acceptance until subsequent gates.",
    "Explain negative-part finiteness is produced through an actual integrable affine lower bound, not assumed. In the finite-positive branch, measurability plus actual finite parts and AE finite embedding produce Integrable Y before using (X,Y) and original nonclosed epigraph membership.",
    "Qualify signedExpectation as total algebraic positive-minus-negative outside admissible inputs. Here the produced finite negative part excludes both-infinite ambiguity; positive-infinite loss expectation is legitimate. Do not promise finite expected loss or use toReal at infinity as a finite loss. The top branch itself supplies only le_top, not an extra mean-domain endpoint.",
    "Keep normalized finite/nonconstant, geometric integrable-input/infinite-square, and nonclosed lower-dimensional probability canaries distinct and quantified accurately; expose two probability instances in later named audit. Counting-measure foundation evidence is not a source probability test.",
    "Update remaining-boundary text to current scoped migration status rather than implying all later subgradient/linearization results are uniformly unproved. Preserve outstanding legacy/source obligations and Chapter2 null/incomplete; two curated teaching links do not claim a full graph export."
  ],
